{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
  "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: I'll repeat myself. I didn't have the mike on. The Court will hear argument in Morgan Stanley Capital Group, Inc., against Snohomish Public Utility District No. 1, or Public District -- Snohomish County No. 1. Mr. Kneedler."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DELLINGER: Justice Stevens, good morning, and may it please the Court: Justice Ginsburg began by asking whether the Ninth Circuit decision did not in fact empower rather than restrict the authority of the Commission. The answer is that the Ninth Circuit decision fundamentally precludes the Commission from carrying out what the Commission believes is essential to its mandate to assure an abundancy of electrical energy at the lowest possible cost."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commission",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They found circumstances where the contracts gave first priority to commercial uses of power, and at a time of shortage that meant that residential customers would be cut off."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You said the Commission is on the job, but one of the pieces of information here is that the Commission staff said that the dysfunction in the spot market carried over into the forward market, such that prices in the forward market were inflated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does it mean that because of the current dysfunction, you can't predict for sure what the rates are going to be down the road?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to start off by picking up on Justice Ginsburg's observation that FERC understood itself to be without discretion here, and add the point that this is an extremely unusual case where FERC thought it lacked discretion to apply the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you acknowledge that that is permissible interpretation of the Federal Power Act or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did these -- did -- did the Petitioners here -- do you claim that the Petitioners here were guilty of failure to report?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WRIGHT",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WRIGHT: Well, Your Honor, again, I\ndon't think we should prevail, and it's not our position\nthat we prevail, unless we show that we didn't have just\nand reasonable alternatives at the time we entered into\nthe contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Are you entitled to relief\nif there was manipulation, but these people were not\nengaging in the manipulation? In other words, they are,\nin effect, innocent of the manipulation; but they, as\nsellers, are in a chaotic market. Are you entitled to\nrelief against them under those circumstances?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WRIGHT",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1457",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a97b1de3046c2150aae3f55b4aa0a60c88a92ba21c8293bfb9c27c499301ba7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a97b1de3046c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a core point of our argument today\nthat that shouldn't be allowed. And I think the answer\nwas: Well, market-based rate authority only results in\nlifting the market-based rate authority; a 206 action\nunder the Federal Power Act is where consumers get\nrelief."
    },
    {
